<title>USA: Neopath shares fall ahead of FDA decision.</title>
<headline>Neopath shares fall ahead of FDA decision.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of NeoPath Inc fell sharply on Friday ahead of a decision by a U.S. Food and Drug Administration panel about the company's AutoPap System.</p>
<p>The system was approved by the FDA last year as a quality control screening device to help detect cervical cancer but the company is also seeking to have the FDA panel approve it as a primary screener of Pap smear slides.</p>
<p>By late afternoon, NeoPath was off 5-1/2 to 23-1/2.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to issue a news release after the hearing is concluded.</p>
</text>
